#: ../../source/cssesc_README.md:54
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cssesc_README.md:56
msgid "`cssesc(value, options)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cssesc_README.md:58
msgid ""
"This function takes a value and returns an escaped version of the value "
"where any characters that are not printable ASCII symbols are escaped "
"using the shortest possible (but valid) [escape sequences for use in CSS "
"strings or identifiers](https://mathiasbynens.be/notes/css-escapes)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cssesc_README.md:68
msgid ""
"By default, `cssesc` returns a string that can be used as part of a CSS "
"string. If the target is a CSS identifier rather than a CSS string, use "
"the `isIdentifier: true` setting (see below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cssesc_README.md:70
msgid ""
"The optional `options` argument accepts an object with the following "
"options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cssesc_README.md:72
msgid "`isIdentifier`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cssesc_README.md:74
msgid ""
"The default value for the `isIdentifier` option is `false`. This means "
"that the input text will be escaped for use in a CSS string literal. If "
"you want to use the result as a CSS identifier instead (in a selector, "
"for example), set this option to `true`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cssesc_README.md:86
msgid "`quotes`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cssesc_README.md:88
msgid ""
"The default value for the `quotes` option is `'single'`. This means that "
"any occurences of `'` in the input text will be escaped as `\\'`, so that"
" the output can be used in a CSS string literal wrapped in single quotes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cssesc_README.md:102
msgid ""
"If you want to use the output as part of a CSS string literal wrapped in "
"double quotes, set the `quotes` option to `'double'`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cssesc_README.md:112
msgid "`wrap`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cssesc_README.md:114
msgid ""
"The `wrap` option takes a boolean value (`true` or `false`), and defaults"
" to `false` (disabled). When enabled, the output will be a valid CSS "
"string literal wrapped in quotes. The type of quotes can be specified "
"through the `quotes` setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cssesc_README.md:132
msgid "`escapeEverything`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cssesc_README.md:134
msgid ""
"The `escapeEverything` option takes a boolean value (`true` or `false`), "
"and defaults to `false` (disabled). When enabled, all the symbols in the "
"output will be escaped, even printable ASCII symbols."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cssesc_README.md:144
msgid "Overriding the default options globally"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cssesc_README.md:146
msgid ""
"The global default settings can be overridden by modifying the "
"`css.options` object. This saves you from passing in an `options` object "
"for every call to `encode` if you want to use the non-default setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cssesc_README.md:161
msgid "`cssesc.version`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cssesc_README.md:163
msgid "A string representing the semantic version number."
msgstr ""

